From: =?UTF-8?q?L=C3=A9onard?= <leonard@synthe.se>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:52:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] MIPS: BMIPS: Select SYS_SUPPORTS_ZBOOT

BMIPS_GENERIC boards boot an ELF image from flash, and the kernel
partition is often small: the AirTies AIR 7310T (BCM7231) leaves 7 MB
to it, which a vmlinux with wireless support outgrows (9 MB stripped),
while the gzip-compressed vmlinuz takes 4 MB. CFE boots the
self-decompressing vmlinuz ELF just like the raw vmlinux.

Select SYS_SUPPORTS_ZBOOT, as other MIPS platforms do. As there, "make"
then builds vmlinuz in addition to vmlinux; vmlinux is unchanged.

Tested on a BCM7231 (BMIPS4380, little endian) booted by CFE.
---
 arch/mips/Kconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/mips/Kconfig b/arch/mips/Kconfig
index d7c67ce..7590d50 100644
--- a/arch/mips/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/Kconfig
@@ -270,6 +270,7 @@ config BMIPS_GENERIC
 	select SYS_SUPPORTS_LITTLE_ENDIAN
 	select SYS_SUPPORTS_BIG_ENDIAN
 	select SYS_SUPPORTS_HIGHMEM
+	select SYS_SUPPORTS_ZBOOT
 	select SYS_HAS_CPU_BMIPS32_3300
 	select SYS_HAS_CPU_BMIPS4350
 	select SYS_HAS_CPU_BMIPS4380
